2|0@PS4^1440541110#cufl8vg:pqowieurytlaksjdhfhg$:Go to the store and search for Headset Companion App, or if you're in the US, get it [here](https://store.playstation.com/#!/en-us/apps/headset-companion-app/cid=UP9000-CUSA00372_00-HEADSETCOMPANION). Once installed, start it on your PS4. Let it download the update then nabigate to your headset. from there go over and select the audio preset you wish to have on your headset. It's a preset to better make use of the headset, specially designed for the Gold headset. There's a few games it supports, but not many.
1|0@PS4^1440785150#cuiviq8:scottyevo$:&gt; it download the update then nabigate to your head Thanks for the comprehensive response. I have downloaded the app and have been using the Until Dawn preset. It's pretty awesome that you can do that. Now I feel obliged to go back and play other games with their audio preset. Any recommendations?
2|0@PS4^1440538482#cufjmv1:digitalskyfire$:Some games have specially designed audio settings for the gold headset, and you can download those settings.
